# Project: FamilyTree

Collaborative family tree viewer/editor. Phone-first, desktop-equal. Static site + Supabase Edge Function. See `docs/PLAN.md` for scope and phases, `docs/DATA_MODEL.md` for the schema.

## JavaScript Module Architecture
- **Configuration**: `/assets/js/config/app-config.js` (`FAMILYTREE_CONFIG.API_URL`, bucket URL base, limits).
- **Utilities**: `/assets/js/utils/` (`api.js`, `tree-access.js` (share code + session token), `gen-date.js` (fuzzy genealogy dates), `kinship.js` (relationship calculator), `image-compress.js`, `brief-message.js`, `confirm-dialog.js`, `formatters.js`, `help-catalog.js`).
- **Components**: `/assets/js/components/` (person-card, person-picker, event-editor, media-uploader, lightbox, pedigree-chart, descendants-chart, fan-chart, timeline, change-log-list, contextual-help).
- **Pages**: `/assets/js/pages/` – one module per HTML page with an `init()`.
- **Entry Point**: `/assets/js/main.js` routes by `document.body.dataset.page`.
- **No Duplication**: common code must live in utils/components, never copied between pages.

## HTML components
- Shared header/nav/footer live in `/components/*.html` and are pasted into each page (no build step). Update the component file first, then propagate to every page.

## Brief message (shared CursorSites pattern)
- Canonical spec: `../cursor-sites-shared/ui/BRIEF_MESSAGE.md` – sync via `../cursor-sites-shared/scripts/sync-ui.ps1`.
- Implementation: `BriefMessage.show(text, anchorEl, options)` in `/assets/js/utils/brief-message.js`; styles in `/assets/css/brief-message.css`.

## Rules for AI (Cursor)
1. **Script loading order**: config → utils → components → pages → main.js.
2. **Relative paths only** (`assets/css/style.css`, not `/assets/...`). Never embed `http://localhost` or drive letters.
3. **Both form factors**: every view must work at 360px wide (phone, touch) and at 1280px+ (desktop, mouse). Charts need pan/zoom by touch and by wheel/drag.
4. **Access**: every API call carries the tree share code; mutations also carry the **session token** (issued at register/connect). The server is the authority – the browser never decides what is private. Passwords, invite codes and session tokens are hashed server-side; never log them.
5. **Living persons**: never render birth dates/places or other private details of a living person unless the server returned them (it only does so for share-code holders).
6. **Attribution**: every mutation writes a `change_log` row (`actor_id` + display name at the time, before/after JSON). Never bypass this. Identity is the `contributors` row, not a device.
7. **Genealogy dates** are fuzzy. Store `date_text` (as typed), `date_sort` (approx date for ordering) and `date_qualifier`. Use `GenDate` helpers; never `new Date(text)` on user dates.
8. **Soft delete**: persons, families, events, media use `deleted_at`; never hard-delete through the API except admin purge.
9. **Images**: compress in the browser with `ImageCompress.compressToTarget` (≈100 KB JPEG) before sending base64 to the API. Never upload originals.
10. **Charts are hand-rolled SVG** (no D3/library). Keep layout code pure (data in → node positions out) in `/assets/js/utils/layout-*.js` so it can be unit-tested with `node --test`.
11. **Design for multiple trees**: every table has `tree_id`; UI is single-tree for now but never hard-code a tree.

## CORS and fetch
12. GET with no custom headers, or POST with `Content-Type: text/plain;charset=UTF-8` and a JSON string body (same as Scrabble/theConfessional). Responses are `{ error: string|null, data: any }`.

## Shared Supabase database (Apps project)
13. This app shares Supabase project `Apps` (`yzyipxvlsoxfphwobfkb`) with other CursorSites apps; our schema is `familytree`, our bucket is `familytree`. Migration history is global – **do not** `supabase db push` or repair/revert other apps' remote migrations.
14. Schema changes: `supabase migration new …`, apply the same SQL with MCP `apply_migration` (schema-qualified), verify with `execute_sql`, commit the file. Edge Function: `supabase functions deploy familytree-api --no-verify-jwt`.
15. Full procedure: `../cursor-sites-shared/supabase/SHARED_DATABASE.md` and `.cursor/rules/supabase-shared-db.mdc`.
